Key improvements:
1. **Faster local search**: instead of trying all (model, GPU) moves and recomputing the full max KVPR for each, we only consider moves off the *worst* GPU and evaluate each candidate with a closed-form new-max computation (only the two affected GPUs change). This is O(models × gpus) per iteration instead of O(models × gpus × gpus) with full recomputation.
2. **Best-improvement moves**: we pick the single best move each iteration rather than the first improving one, which typically converges to a better local optimum.
3. **Simpler code**: the swap phase (which was expensive and rarely fired) is removed, reducing complexity while keeping solution quality via the 8 diverse greedy starts.
